// A method that is not a Cedar built-in AND whose receiver chain does not
// bottom out at a declared-provider invocation must be rejected.
//
// Before the provider-path unification the parser hard-errored on any
// unknown method at parse time. Now the parser defers such a method as an
// `ExprKind::MethodCall`, and lowering resolves it: a provider chain is
// hoisted, anything else is an "unknown method" error. This case guards
// that the deferred error still fires — the receiver here is a plain
// context field (`context.input.document`), not a provider, so
// `.footgun()` has no meaning and lowering must reject it.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when {
    context.input.document.footgun() == true
};
